    "doc_text": "AFP_ENG_19970424.0028\n\nBEIJING, April 24 , 1997 (AFP)\n\nTaiwan PC giant to launch cellular phone production in China: report\n\n\n\n\nTaiwan-based personal computer giant Acer Inc. will begin producing GSM cellular telephones in eastern China's Suzhou next month, the China Daily reported Thursday.\n\nThe rollout by 30-million-dollar venture Acer Peripherals (Suzhou) Co. will mark the firm's first mainland production of GSM (global system for mobile communications) handsets, it said, quoting a company official.\n\nThough it is already deeply involved in the Chinese PC market, Acer plans to strengthen its presence in the country's booming telecom market.\n\nIt is developing a new cellular phone using Chinese-developed technology, the report said.\n\nAcer, the world's seventh largest computer maker, reported last month that its net profit slumped 44 percent from a year earlier to 3.06 billion Taiwan dollars (111.1 million US) in 1996.",
